  <section class="page">
    <article class="content-block">
      <h2>Next Up and playlist synchronization</h2>
      <p>In builds with media context menus, long press a title to add it to Next Up, a playlist or a collection. Within a group, Remove from the named group preserves media files and watched history. Movies and episodes offer Mark Watched and Mark Unwatched; both reset the item's resume position and update its finished status in Jellyfin. Removing a media item from Next Up also clears its Jellyfin Continue Watching position and local resume checkpoint without marking it watched. The dismissal stays on the current device/account until the item is explicitly added or played again. Mark Watched removes the item; Mark Unwatched alone does not restore it. Active playlists represent their individual members, except an unfinished earlier episode skipped by the playlist.</p>
      <p>For builds with native Jellyfin lists, see the <a href="https://github.com/eslutz/A-Playa-Named-Gus/wiki/Next-Up-and-Playlists">Next Up, Playlists and Collections guide</a> and the <a href="https://github.com/eslutz/A-Playa-Named-Gus/wiki/Collections">Collections guide</a>. Jellyfin owns playlist and collection names, membership, playlist order and permissions. Gus caches playlists by server/user and saves playlist edits until it can contact Jellyfin. Collections appear within Movies, have artwork and membership links, and require an online connection for edits. Collection editing is permission-gated and unavailable on Apple TV. Collections group titles; all-video playlists support ordered video playback, existing audio playlists open the audio player, and mixed-media entries open individually.</p>
      <p>In builds with the updated playlist controls, open More → Edit. Administrators can choose Change Cover, preview the image, and select Save to update the shared cover in Jellyfin. Other users can still edit playlist entries where their account allows it. On eligible playlists, Next Up, Start from Beginning and Shuffle appear below Play or Resume.</p>
      <p>Home Next Up sorts by recent activity. Optional private iCloud synchronization carries Gus resume positions, Next Up intent and activity; it requires the same iCloud account and independent sign-in to the same Jellyfin server/user on each device. When iCloud sync is disabled, iCloud account changes leave local saved data visible. The first verified identity preserves current local saved-queue order; later accounts remain isolated. Native lists come from Jellyfin, pending server edits stay on their originating device, and downloaded files remain device-local. The refinement candidate removes retired Gus-only playlist imports and old queue formats without importing that data; current Jellyfin playlists, offline drafts and supplemental state remain supported. Jellyfin 10.11.11 accepts each media item once per native playlist.</p>
      <p>If a playlist edit needs review, refresh and inspect Jellyfin before explicitly retrying or discarding it: a create/add request may have succeeded even when its response was lost. Collection changes remain online-only; the refinement candidate requires a fresh server snapshot and Use Current Server State after an uncertain result before another edit. A missing video-playlist item can be retried, skipped, or explicitly replaced without deleting your underlying media. Signed iCloud provisioning and physical cross-device validation remain pending for this feature branch.</p>
    </article>
